me><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Westborn</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Kallen</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Congenital malformations among infants whose mothers had gestational diabetes or preexisting diabetes</article-title><source>Early Hum Dev</source><year>2001</year><volume>61</volume><fpage>85</fpage><lpage>95</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11223271</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0378-3782(00)00125-0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Martinez-Frias</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Bermejo</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Cereijo</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Preaxial polydactyly of feet in infants of diabetic mothers: epidemiological test of a clinical hypothesis</article-title><source>Am J Med Genet</source><year>1992</year><volume>42</volume><fpage>643</fpage><lpage>646</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1632430</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/ajmg.1320420502</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Slee</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldblatt</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Further evidence ofor preaxial hallucal polydactyly as a marker of diabetic embryopathy</article-title><source>J Med Genet</source><year>1997</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>261</fpage><lpage>263</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9132503</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Joshi</surname><given-names>RR</given-names></name><name><surname>Rao</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Desai</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Etiology and clinical profile of ambiguous genitalia-an overview of 10 years experience</article-title><source>Indian Pediatr</source><year>2006</year><volume>43</volume><fpage>974</fpage><lpage>979</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17151400</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Falhammar</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Filipsson</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Holmdahl</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Janson</surname><given-names>PO</given-names></name><name><surname>Nordenskjold</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hagenfeldt</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Thoren</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Metabolic profile and body composition in adult women with congenital adrenal hyperplasia due to 21-hydroxylase deficiency</article-title><source>J Clin Endocrinol Metab</source><year>2007</year><volume>92</volume><fpage>110</fpage><lpage>116</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17032717</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1210/jc.2006-1350</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>